      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "The magnetic susceptibility $\\chi$ of a paramagnetic material varies with absolute temperature $T$ according to:",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "$\\chi \\propto \\frac{1}{T}$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "$\\chi \\propto T$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "$\\chi \\propto T^2$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "$\\chi$ is independent of $T$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "According to Curie's Law, the magnetic susceptibility of a paramagnetic material is inversely proportional to its absolute temperature, i.e., $\\chi = \\frac{C}{T}$."
    },
    {
      "ref": "PHY-MGM-002",
      "subtopic": "magnetic-properties-of-materials",
      "type": "single_correct",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "expected_time_sec": 45,
      "source_type": "pyq",
      "exam": "jee_main",
      "year": 2022,
      "shift": "25 Jul 2022, Shift 1",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "The magnetic susceptibility of a paramagnetic material at $-73^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ is $0.0075$. Its value at $127^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ will be:",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "$0.00375$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "$0.0050$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "$0.0150$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "$0.0075$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "According to Curie's Law, susceptibility $\\chi \\propto \\frac{1}{T}$, where $T$ is in Kelvin.\n$T_1 = -73 + 273 = 200\\ \\mathrm{K}$, $T_2 = 127 + 273 = 400\\ \\mathrm{K}$.\n$\\frac{\\chi_2}{\\chi_1} = \\frac{T_1}{T_2} = \\frac{200}{400} = \\frac{1}{2}$.\n$\\chi_2 = \\frac{0.0075}{2} = 0.00375$."
    }
  ]
